  gsmin:statusnotes "Mining of the mineral goes back to Egyptian times, and the mineral name predates a formal description. For instance, the name appears in the medical literature: Wallerius J G (1741) Sal natron, in Decades Binae Thesium Medicarum, J A Darellius (Upsaliæ) 29-31 The mineral is described: Wallerius J G (1750) I. Mit Erdevermischtes alkalisches Salz. Species 189. Alkali orientale impurum terrestre. Natron. Nitrum veterum, in Mineralogie,oder Mineralreich, Nicolai (Berlin) 228-228"@en ;
  gsmin:strunzcodeV10 "05.CB.10" ;
  gsmin:strunzlabel "Carbonate without additional anions, with H2O, With large cations (alkali and alkali-earth carbonates)"@en ;
  gsmin:webmineralurl "http://www.webmineral.com/data/Natron.shtml" ;
  gsmin:wikipediadate "1783" ;
