gsmin:smectitegroup
  rdf:type owl:Class ;
  rdfs:comment "Smectite a group name for platy phyllosilicates of 2:1 layer and a layer charge of ~ -0.2 to -0.6 per formula unit. Generally for natural samples, the d(001) spacing is approximately 14.4-15.6 Å, although other spacing may occur depending on H2O retention and interlayer occupancy. The group is further divided into subgroups that are either trioctahedral (according to Bailey, 1980, this subgroup name is saponite) or dioctahedral (subgroup name of montmorillonite, according to Bailey, 1980), and these subgroups are further divided into mineral species.  Prior to circa 1975, the smectite group was called the montmorillonite-saponite group"@en ;
  rdfs:label "Smectite"@en ;
  rdfs:subClassOf gsog:Mineral_Material ;
  rdfs:subClassOf gsmin:claymineral ;
  gsmin:mindatid "min-11119" ;
.
